1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,120
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,221
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:07,760
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,937
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,440
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:15,697
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,820
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,217
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,297
We came to this new world believing.

11
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:37,957
That surely someday we
just might find the way.

12
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,297
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,217
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:16,997
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,757
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:23,180
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,840
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,857
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,637
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,157
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,877
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,860
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:14,317
Only look up, keep your
head up way up high.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,937
Always step up, if brains
are rubbed up to the sky.

50
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,677
Never give up, our wishes
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,057
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:31,920
Alright, fire!

54
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:35,130
God!

55
00:02:35,213 --> 00:02:36,117
That's way too many!

56
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,640
No Gum-Gum!

57
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:41,180
Legs full! Boot! Now what?

58
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:42,860
No more legs!

59
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,740
Devil Fruit.

60
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:49,560
Ha-ha-ha!

61
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,780
I know just the thing for you!

62
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,800
Now fire! Fire!

63
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:11,552
Aim right for the bottom of their vessel.

64
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:13,300
Come on, let's turn back.

65
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,401
Like I would ever do that, Usopp.

66
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:18,480
Go forward!

67
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,060
Oh, I'm sorry.

68
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:22,574
Did you not notice the nonstop gunfire?

69
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:25,600
I told you!

70
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:28,407
We're this close to
sinking to a watery calf!

71
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,380
Ha ha ha!

72
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:34,200
You'll never escape the wrath
of Brownbeard, you fools!

73
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:38,226
I'm the former pirate with a
bounty of over 80 million berries!

74
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,380
Fair enough.

75
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:44,440
But you won't forget this.

76
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:52,060
No way! He got us! We're falling!

77
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:55,700
This is bad.

78
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,880
Ha! That's all it, teacher.

79
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:02,020
Real nice shot there, boss.

80
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:03,920
They're dead meat now.

81
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,820
It serves you right.

82
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:11,960
Struggling won't help you.

83
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:14,829
Soon you'll all freeze
and think like rots.

84
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:20,880
So cold. It's over.

85
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:23,880
We're gonna be the snow cones. This blows.

86
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:26,900
This is all your fault, Luffy.

87
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:28,820
We could have got away.

88
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:32,920
But, oh, you just had to keep on
putting his butt in, didn't you?

89
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:34,900
Oh, no.

90
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:37,160
I can't even talk now.

91
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,620
I'm sorry. Oh, well.

92
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:42,480
I guess they won't join
the crew after all.

93
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:44,540
Now, finish them off!

94
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:48,040
Now, here's what we'll do.

95
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:51,040
You stay and keep them from drowning.

96
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:52,400
I'll get slicing.

97
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:53,600
Be right back.

98
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,340
Make it quick.

99
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:58,357
I don't know how, but...

100
00:04:58,440 --> 00:04:59,840
It'll just take a sec.

101
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,060
Zoro, are you okay?

102
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:12,390
Hey!

103
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:14,880
Why are there sharks in a lake?

104
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:17,680
It's simple.

105
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:19,900
That's not a lake. It's a sea.

106
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:25,600
The battle between Akainu and Aokiji was
so explosive, it left a massive crater.

107
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,277
Water from the sea
poured in through cracks

108
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:31,280
in the island and made what you see here.

109
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:34,440
It brought plenty of
sea life along with it.

110
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:44,920
Ah, no, no kidding, Zoro,
also hurry, I'm cold.

111
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:50,957
Aim and fire, there's
nowhere they can go now.

112
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:53,420
Hate to say it, but he's right!

113
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,708
Send them straight to hell!

114
00:05:56,140 --> 00:06:01,081
After all the crazy crap I've lived through,
this is the thing that's gonna kill me!

115
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,480
Now meet your maker!

116
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,430
Fire!

117
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,340
My soldiers.

118
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:20,328
What just happened to them?

119
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:24,080
I think I know!

120
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:30,677
Colder than a blizzard,

121
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:36,780
the wind from the underworld
cuts like an icy blade.

122
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:39,140
Damn you!

123
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,780
What is this?

124
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:49,480
By the way, I just froze your gun barrels,
so I would advise against shooting.

125
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:53,992
Unless you want them to explode, that is.

126
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:55,637
Who the hell are you?

127
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:57,485
And why the skeleton disguise?

128
00:06:57,820 --> 00:07:00,960
My name is of no consequence. It's Brook.

129
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,439
Make up your mind.

130
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:05,200
I died once and became a skeleton.

131
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:10,740
And now that I live again, my second
life is devoted to the Straw Hat crew!

132
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:15,800
You can call me the Soul King.

133
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,240
I don't know how you froze our guns.

134
00:07:21,340 --> 00:07:23,300
But... you'll pay! Pay?

135
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:25,740
And how do you plan to make me?

136
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:30,280
Bastard! That's it!

137
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:37,020
I've lost enough friends
in my time, so I say...

138
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:38,960
No way!

139
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:43,380
What the hell?

140
00:07:43,660 --> 00:07:45,300
He's so fast, it's scary!

141
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:47,800
They beat up the Sharks?

142
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:50,490
What?

143
00:07:50,573 --> 00:07:52,378
Where did those wretched pirates go?

144
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,380
Right here.

145
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:01,840
This is a pleasant surprise, Brooke!

146
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,697
It's so good to see you all.

147
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:08,457
Who knew running from
that terrifying ghost

148
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:10,952
would lead me directly to where you were?

149
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:13,777
Centaurs, dragons, sharks.

150
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:16,357
I don't care what this
island throws at us!

151
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:18,697
You should have run
while you had the chance,

152
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:21,074
because you sure as hell can't stop us.

153
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:29,200
But this damn weather,
that's another thing.

154
00:08:29,420 --> 00:08:32,220
I can't cut that with
my sword. It's freezing.

155
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:34,080
I can barely walk.

156
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,377
I told you guys, don't you remember?

157
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:39,989
We can't just go to the cold
side like this, I said, but no.

158
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,560
Hey, look over there.

159
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:44,300
If you ask me, we got lucky.

160
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:49,087
Running into them was the best
thing that could have happened.

161
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,150
They're close.

162
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:51,281
Let's open fire.

163
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:53,890
Hold on.

164
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:55,865
I think I've seen them before.

165
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:58,180
Good thinking, Robin.

166
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:01,120
I called the fourth guy from the right.

167
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,000
Yeah, nice one.

168
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:06,220
I'll take the guy next to him.

169
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:08,528
All right, now, let me see.

170
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,700
The girl on the far left will do nicely.

171
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:13,170
Huh?

172
00:09:13,253 --> 00:09:14,083
I'm confused.

173
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:24,177
Those coats look nice and warm.

174
00:09:24,260 --> 00:09:26,097
All right, good idea.

175
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:28,837
But please get me wiped out!

176
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:32,780
Uh-oh, they're not going to
take our clothes, are they?

177
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:35,820
No way, then we'll freeze to death.

178
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:41,180
I remember now, that Straw Hat.

179
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:47,877
Yes, from two years ago.

180
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:50,200
That came from the worst generation.

181
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,660
There's no doubt.

182
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,500
That's Firefist's brother.

183
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:59,457
The pirates draw at Luffy.

184
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:02,120
With a 400 million bounty.

185
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:04,950
What?

186
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:06,940
He's gonna kill us all

187
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,520
Please don't hurt me!

188
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:19,960
Come on, kids.

189
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:21,905
Let's karate chop our way out.

190
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,833
Where's that back door?

191
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,181
Hold your treat.

192
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:27,780
We mustn't go.

193
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:31,317
That fellow back there was the
one that cut my body into three.

194
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:32,230
No way.

195
00:10:32,313 --> 00:10:33,143
Seriously?

196
00:10:33,226 --> 00:10:36,740
So, do you think he might still
have the rest of you? On hand?

197
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:41,940
I highly doubt he would. Okay,
then. It can wait. Take me back.

198
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:44,257
Perhaps I can obtain some information.

199
00:10:44,340 --> 00:10:48,869
The only relevant information right now
is that we need to run the hell away.

200
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:55,000
That was the samurai.

201
00:10:58,500 --> 00:10:59,900
And the Straw Hats.

202
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,765
I'm not letting them get away.

203
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,450
Room.

204
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,402
Hey, did you guys just see that?

205
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:11,795
The air is all perky.

206
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:19,380
All right, shambles.

207
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,350
whoa!

208
00:11:38,433 --> 00:11:39,757
I just felt something weird!

209
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,317
No time to think about it right now!

210
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:44,117
Keep moving! rug rats!

211
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,477
The exit can't be far!

212
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:47,617
What the hell?

213
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:48,817
My cigarette go

214
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:55,900
super

215
00:11:57,060 --> 00:12:00,397
close to!

216
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:01,697
busting our way out of here!

217
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:02,610
I can feel it!

218
00:12:02,693 --> 00:12:03,523
Good thing!

219
00:12:03,606 --> 00:12:04,436
I got these Tribe power!

220
00:12:04,519 --> 00:12:06,557
Tank transit crap!

221
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:09,860
You're acting really weird!

222
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:15,077
that ability is way too powerful! Yeah!

223
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:16,857
That guy really creeps me out!

224
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:18,357
I don't think so!

225
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:21,000
None of you are going anywhere!

226
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:34,197
He turned our ship into
abstract art! It's a wreck!

227
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:36,600
We can't take that out to sea! I know!

228
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:39,637
We're stuck on this crappy
island with that lunatic!

229
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,737
You work for the government too, bud!

230
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:45,055
And just now, you broke
contract by causing us trouble!

231
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:46,834
Yeah, cut it out, Law!

232
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,320
Wait till we tell HQ!

233
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:50,446
You're gonna lose your title!

234
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:53,640
See how much I care.

235
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:56,040
Now scan.

236
00:12:57,540 --> 00:12:59,640
What's that do? Oh, no!

237
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:05,590
Huh?

238
00:13:05,673 --> 00:13:06,503
Transponder snails?

239
00:13:06,586 --> 00:13:08,040
Wait, I lost mine!

240
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:09,520
Whoa, so did I!

241
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:12,680
Hey, you stole them, didn't you?

242
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:14,040
Give those back!

243
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:15,437
What do you need them for, huh?

244
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:18,317
I can't let you reveal what
you've seen on this island.

245
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:21,720
This way, the government
never has to hear about it.

246
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:33,120
Warlord or not, you've
pushed your luck too far now.

247
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:40,200
The abob fruit, huh?

248
00:13:40,580 --> 00:13:42,227
Let's see what it's made of.

249
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:47,308
Don't let him cut you, man.

250
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:48,400
Just stay away.

251
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:52,630
He's happy!

252
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,310
What the?

253
00:13:58,440 --> 00:13:59,860
I don't need you here.

254
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:01,517
Get outside of the circle.

255
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:02,659
Wait, what circle?

256
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,637
Look, as long as you're in this vicinity,

257
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:08,308
you're like a patient
on an operating table.

258
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:10,157
Law is the surgeon of death.

259
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:13,700
He can control anything within
his operating room at will.

260
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,720
He'll end you!

261
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,520
Trafalgar Law!

262
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:23,260
You've left me no choice!

263
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:25,860
Stop to see him! You can't win!

264
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,313
Your hockey's too weak!

265
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:35,500
No, it can't be!

266
00:14:40,820 --> 00:14:41,650
Huh?

267
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,480
You cut her clean in
half, you sick bastard!

268
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:51,000
Hey, uh, you're still alive, right?

269
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:52,320
Say something!

270
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:04,930
Pathetic.

271
00:15:05,013 --> 00:15:08,520
Flying here in pieces, cut
down but left to live in shame.

272
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:15,380
Why won't you finish me, Trafalgar?

273
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:24,392
You may wield a sword, but
don't act like you're a master.

274
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:28,180
Honor is something that
you earn, not beg for.

275
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:34,260
Weaklings like you don't get
to choose where they die.

276
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:38,470
Enough!

277
00:15:38,553 --> 00:15:40,300
Your sword can't even reach me.

278
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:41,880
Don't bother.

279
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:51,032
You still want to fight?

280
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:52,927
I can chop you up some more.

281
00:15:57,340 --> 00:15:58,180
Stand back!

282
00:15:58,420 --> 00:16:01,537
If you lay another finger on
our captain, we'll mess you up!

283
00:16:01,620 --> 00:16:03,149
Hey, captain, don't worry.

284
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:07,145
We'll see how cocky this bastard
is after we fill him with land!

285
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:13,140
What the hell?

286
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,357
How is he shooting at us?

287
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:17,616
I don't see any gun!

288
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,717
We shot him and he didn't even bunch!

289
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:22,417
You shot at yourselves,
you bunch of imbeciles.

290
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:25,206
I switched your bullets
with the falling snow.

291
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:26,830
Ha ha!

292
00:16:26,913 --> 00:16:27,743
Hey, he's cheating!

293
00:16:27,826 --> 00:16:28,656
That isn't fair!

294
00:16:29,540 --> 00:16:30,380
Get down!

295
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,617
He'll take your head clean off, man!

296
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,257
He cut a damn ship in half!

297
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:35,752
You can't stop this guy!

298
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:37,680
He's too strong!

299
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:39,469
Get out of there, Captain!

300
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:44,880
Captain, no!

301
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:57,090
Yeah!

302
00:16:57,173 --> 00:16:58,300
Captain Smokey!

303
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:04,100
You may be a warlord, but
you're still just a pirate.

304
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:20,900
That weapon you're swinging around,
it's tipped with sea prism stone.

305
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:23,145
I could feel it in an instant.

306
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:33,120
His ice sculpture!

307
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:35,204
I mean our ship is coming down!

308
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:37,940
I think that's our cue to run away!

309
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:39,889
We can't fight him anyway!

310
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:41,740
We got no business here!

311
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,400
You'll be okay!

312
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:46,997
There's nothing we can do!

313
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:48,077
It's our fight!

314
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:49,817
I'm telling you, we're
dead weight right now!

315
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:50,730
Weight blow!

316
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:55,660
Out of the circle!

317
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:57,234
Get out of the circle!

318
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,180
That noise sure was loud, huh?

319
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,840
I bet it was Saint.

320
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:17,237
Hey, Krakatar, you still don't want to
tell me where the rest of my crew is at?

321
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:20,577
Keep dreaming, but you're not gonna
get a word out of me, all right?

322
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:23,717
We gotta get to that big building
before someone gets hurt.

323
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:24,630
Like me?

324
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:26,180
Or my crew you robbed?

325
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:29,957
You're nothing but a bunch of thugs.

326
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:32,452
And now you gotta humiliate me like this.

327
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:35,840
Man up, man-a-dial, crack-o-man, whatever.

328
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,477
Brooke, you don't even have skin.

329
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:41,257
You're sitting there shivering,
but you can't be cold, right?

330
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:43,857
Did you just steal that coat
because you wanted to fit in?

331
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:44,920
What if I did?

332
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:47,017
We've been able to keep ourselves warm,

333
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:49,457
but I fear the others
might not be so fortunate.

334
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:52,497
If they get frostbite, they
could lose any number of limbs.

335
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:53,410
That's enough!

336
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:56,169
Just spare us your
gruesome concerns, okay?

337
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:01,069
What should we do, Master?

338
00:19:01,660 --> 00:19:04,719
Law and Smoker are having
an Alto battle outside.

339
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:10,160
Law has made a nuisance of himself.

340
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:12,997
He was supposed to make
them leave peacefully.

341
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:17,397
Also, the pirates took the children from
the biscuit room with them to the front.

342
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:20,917
They ran into Law, but it doesn't look
like they're part of the struggle.

343
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:25,040
Wait, that means that the Navy
saw the children? Yes, sir.

344
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:27,380
That was the last thing I wanted.

345
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:32,022
They might not know what, but now
they know we're up to something.

346
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:36,400
At this point, even if we kill Smoker,

347
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:39,657
the Navy will only send more
Marines to investigate us.

348
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:40,780
I thought so.

349
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:45,466
I hope you have something helpful
to contribute to this, Monet.

350
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:48,140
I know who our intruders are.

351
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,320
Never mind, Smoker.

352
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,989
We should have kept a
tartar leash on them.

353
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:55,160
Oh, right.

354
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,242
I guess I neglected to tell you.

355
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:58,851
They already took out Dr.

356
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,397
Vegapunk's dragon, as well as
Brownbeard's centaur patrol unit.

357
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:04,040
They did what? How?

358
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:07,677
The people that you kidnapped
weren't their only crew members,

359
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:09,777
just the only crew members on the ship.

360
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:12,860
The rest had already set
off for the Burning Lands.

361
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:15,264
They've since crossed the lake.

362
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:17,792
I imagine they'll be here any minute now.

363
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,310
Huh?

364
00:20:19,393 --> 00:20:22,320
At least we know who we're
dealing with. You see?

365
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:25,996
There's no doubting it's them, right?

366
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:27,960
The faces match.

367
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:29,490
That's true.

368
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:35,540
So long, ship.

369
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:36,977
There's no fixing that.

370
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:38,117
Got your legs back yet?

371
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,677
You're not in any pain now, are you?

372
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:41,697
Hey, you got a foot on
your wrist there, pal.

373
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:43,217
You're gonna want to take care of that.

374
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:44,130
Huh?

375
00:20:44,213 --> 00:20:45,200
Oh, geez, you're right.

376
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:47,397
I don't even know who
this foot belongs to.

377
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:48,310
Damn it!

378
00:20:48,393 --> 00:20:50,320
We can't even contact HQ anymore!

379
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:53,557
We're stranded on this
crappy island! Law's a jerk!

380
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:55,993
I thought the warlords were on our side!

381
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:02,597
There's one thing you always
need to remember, Toshiki.

382
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:03,980
A pirate's a pirate.

383
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:06,609
No matter where they
go, they never change.

384
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:12,800
All warlords are the same. He was right.

385
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:47,100
This plan must be why you joined up
with the seven warlords, isn't it?

386
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:49,382
But what the hell are you after?

387
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:07,440
I don't know.

388
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:29,477
I've never been a fan
of the Warlord system.

389
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:32,384
Pirates can't be trusted
no matter who they are.

390
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,460
You got that one right.

391
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:06,080
There's something big going on here.

392
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:12,917
And you're only part of it—who is it?

393
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,760
Who's running this show? First.

394
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:26,510
First

395
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:33,100
What's your story?

396
00:23:33,300 --> 00:23:34,712
What are you doing here?

397
00:23:53,900 --> 00:23:56,077
If you want to get to
the bottom of something,

398
00:23:56,160 --> 00:24:00,600
then you've got to broaden your
horizons, or you'll miss the truth.

399
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:03,900
Scalpel.

400
00:24:23,140 --> 00:24:25,040
My heart.

401
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:44,180
You can beg, but I don't have
to tell you a damn thing.

402
00:25:01,780 --> 00:25:02,610
Thank you.
